            <div xml:id="d180">

                <pb facs="0739" n="710" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v28/pg710"/>

                <head>180. Briefing Memorandum From the Under Secretary of State for Management
                    (Read) to Secretary of State Muskie<anchor n="1" xml:id="d180-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1980-09-09">September 9, 1980</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Professional Development Group to Vet FSI Proposal</item>
                </list>
                <p>As a result of our Saturday morning meeting on the budget,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d180-f2"/> I am forming an assistant-secretary level group to go
                    over the structure and content of the career development and training proposal
                    in our FY 82 budget request. The group’s mission will be to give the proposal a
                    strenuous vetting, drawing on its own and outsiders’ perspective, to make sure
                    the nature, timing and amount of training presented to OMB later this month are
                    solidly grounded and backed by the career service. The group will meet twice
                    weekly over the next three weeks, starting Thursday, September 11, bringing in
                    outside advice as necessary.</p>
                <pb facs="0740" n="711" xml:id="pg711"/>
                <p>I am asking the following to join this group, which I will chair:</p>
                <p>Matt Nimetz, Under Secretary</p>
                <p>Roz Ridgway, Counselor</p>
                <p> Harry Barnes, Director General</p>
                <p> Ron Spiers, Assistant Secretary, INR </p>
                <p>Diego Asencio, Assistant Secretary, CA </p>
                <p> Tom Tracy, Assistant Secretary, A</p>
                <p>Deane Hinton, Assistant Secretary, EB </p>
                <p> Hal Saunders, Assistant Secretary, NEA </p>
                <p> Tony Lake, Director, S/P </p>
                <p>Roger Feldman, Comptroller</p>
                <p>Paul Boeker, Director, FSI </p>
                <p>Vivian Derryck, Deputy Assistant Secretary-designate, Equal Employment
                    Opportunity</p>
                <p> Bray, ICA </p>
                <p> James Isbister, ICA </p>


                <xi:include href="d180-a1.xml" xpointer="d180-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
